WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
Two classes sit the same maths test.

2
00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.860
Both have a mean mark
of sixty-two per cent.

3
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.400
The pass mark is fifty per cent.

4
00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.910
Yet one class has far
more fails than the other.

5
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.100
Same test, same mean.

6
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.660
So what could be different?

7
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.070
Is one class bigger?

8
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.020
Is one median lower?

9
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.310
In this mission, you'll compare data sets
with a measure of location and a measure

10
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.490
of spread.

11
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.870
You'll calculate the standard deviation,
roughly the typical distance of a value

12
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.050
from the mean.

13
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:33.870
And you'll use quartiles,
and spot possible outliers.

14
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.350
Your mission: explain why one
class might have far more fails.
